C1 -- mu^-1(c_ad) and the published lensing / cluster bounds translated into c_ad
================================================================================================================
  ambient dust density = cosmic mean rho_d = 2.270e-27 kg/m^3 (the dust does not cluster on galaxy scales, L153b)
   c_ad km/s  mu^-1 Mpc  mu^2 Mpc^-2
          42       0.99       1.0275
         100       2.35       0.1813
         200       4.70       0.0453
         300       7.05       0.0201
         450      10.57       0.0090
         537      12.61       0.0063
        1000      23.49       0.0018
        1340      31.47       0.0010
  MMH2023 Table 1 (m^2/f_G = mu^2):  <~ 1 Mpc^-2 (WL, a_b >= 1e-13)  =>  c_ad >= 43 km/s
                                     <~ 1e-3 Mpc^-2 (WL, a_b >= 1e-15) =>  c_ad >= 1346 km/s
                                     >~ 2.5 Mpc^-2 (clusters via mu)   =>  c_ad <= 27 km/s  [superseded: L153b captures clusters nonlinearly]
  [PASS] C1-1  mu^-1 = 7.1 Mpc at c_ad = 300 km/s and scales linearly with c_ad: the Helmholtz scale is a cosmological length for every c_ad in the L153b window (>= 3.5 Mpc at 150 km/s)   (mu^-1(300) = 7.05 Mpc)
  [PASS] C1-2  the published loose lensing bound (mu^2 <~ 1 Mpc^-2) is c_ad >= 42 km/s -- below the L153b floor, not binding; the deep bound (mu^2 <~ 1e-3, a_b >= 1e-15, which MMH2023 flag as less reliable) would be c_ad >= 1340 km/s, ABOVE the arXiv:1601.05097 ceiling of 537 km/s -- so the deep lensing points alone would close the window if their isolation criterion is trusted   (c_loose = 43, c_deep = 1346 km/s)
  [PASS] C1-3  and the MMH pincer's CLUSTER horn (mu^2 >~ 2.5 Mpc^-2 <=> c_ad <= 27 km/s) does not apply to the transplant: clusters are filled by the nonlinear exponential capture (L153b B2-3), not by the linear mu-term -- the linear pincer is an artefact of quadratic K   (c_clus = 27 km/s)

